1
00:00:00,256 --> 00:00:04,693
Choose a supported ZTF one point x workflow or script and its matching

2
00:00:04,693 --> 00:00:08,568
configuration. A filename alone does not select the action.

3
00:00:08,789 --> 00:00:13,490
For example, a PC registration file is not a storage-standard configuration.

4
00:00:13,641 --> 00:00:18,078
Retired Native, NKP and two point x execution routes do not

5
00:00:18,078 --> 00:00:19,791
provide an alternative launcher.

6
00:00:20,041 --> 00:00:24,556
For Cluster A, verify the actual target and purpose of every credential

7
00:00:24,649 --> 00:00:29,160
reference. Group labels make the list easier to navigate but never substitute

8
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:32,971
the correct account. Save changed values to ZTF.

9
00:00:33,171 --> 00:00:36,883
A reference being present is different from the target accepting its username

10
00:00:36,883 --> 00:00:41,247
and password. When changing administrative access, review the exact

11
00:00:41,297 --> 00:00:42,783
scope and confirmation.

12
00:00:43,047 --> 00:00:47,383
Verify replacement authentication before later configuration stages use it.

13
00:00:47,510 --> 00:00:52,118
Do not automatically replay a failed password-change step: a request can

14
00:00:52,118 --> 00:00:55,462
succeed remotely even when the following verification fails.

15
00:00:55,816 --> 00:01:00,041
Set Prism Login Title changes the PE login-screen title, not

16
00:01:00,041 --> 00:01:03,617
the cluster, controller virtual machine or hypervisor name.

17
00:01:03,795 --> 00:01:07,789
Local administrator scripts need independent user and role verification.

18
00:01:08,043 --> 00:01:11,790
Keep version-specific prerequisites and approval policy with the selected action

19
00:01:11,969 --> 00:01:14,876
rather than assuming every script shares the same contract.

20
00:01:15,211 --> 00:01:19,630
Read the saved job output, reported stage and safe diagnostic.

21
00:01:19,798 --> 00:01:24,035
Distinguish credential resolution, rejected authentication, permissions,

22
00:01:24,107 --> 00:01:26,190
transport and response validation.

23
00:01:26,411 --> 00:01:30,830
Reconcile the actual target state before requesting another approved attempt.

24
00:01:31,041 --> 00:01:35,515
A successful process exit alone is not complete operational acceptance.
